<title>ITALY: May air cargo at Rome airports fell 2.2pct.</title>
<headline>May air cargo at Rome airports fell 2.2pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rome airport operator said May air cargo at Fiumicino Leonardo de Vinci and Ciampino airports, fell 2.2 percent to 22,748 tonnes against the same period 1996. Mail at the Rome airports rose 3.7 percent against the same period 1996.</p>
<p>Cargo and mail handled by the two airports in tonnes with the percentage change was as follows, official figure showed. May 1997</p>
<p>		  Cargo    pct change     Mail	pct change</p>
<p>Fiumicino     21,953   down  2.9	3,483     up  3.7</p>
<p>Ciampino	   795     up 18.1	    0     n/a</p>
<p>Total	   22,748   down  2.2	3,483     up  3.7</p>
<p>Jan/May 97</p>
<p>		  Cargo    pct change     Mail	pct change</p>
<p>Fiumicino     98,547   down  9.9    17,596	up  8.7</p>
<p>Ciampino	 3,946     up 26.7	   0	   n/a</p>
<p>Total	  102,483   down  8.9    17,596	up 10.0</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
